","Food-safe","Dishwasher-safe"],"careNote":"Dishwasher-safe on a gentle cycle. Skip scouring pads on the bare rim, a soft cloth keeps it smooth.","batchSize":14,"stock":6,"releasedAt":"2026-09-26"},{"id":"46688f4d-80e1-404c-bd6c-c1597ed6c195","slug":"ember-cup","number":3,"name":"Ember Cup","category":"cups","glazeName":"Oxide brown","glazeColor":"#4E2A18","rimColor":"#B5603C","form":"cup","finish":"gloss","speckled":false,"price":32,"dimensions":"Ø 85 × 95 mm","weight":"0.3 kg","description":"A straight-sided cup that sits warm in the hand, sized for a long coffee or a pot of tea poured slowly. The oxide brown glaze breaks to warm terracotta at the rim, where iron rises through the firing. No handle, just a thick wall that holds the heat.","materialNotes":["Wheel-thrown stoneware","Iron oxide gloss glaze","Holds 250 ml","Food-safe","Dishwasher and microwave safe"],"careNote":"Dishwasher and microwave safe. Let it cool before rinsing in cold water, stoneware dislikes sudden changes.","batchSize":14,"stock":6,"releasedAt":"2026-10-03"},{"id":"7dacd408-42fb-40e2-8024-8c080f57d47c","slug":"hollow-jug","number":4,"name":"Hollow Jug","category":"vases","glazeName":"Charcoal black","glazeColor":"#1F1B19","rimColor":null,"form":"jug","finish":"matte","speckled":false,"price":74,"dimensions":"Ø 160 × 210 mm","weight":"1.2 kg","description":"A round-bellied jug with a pinched spout and a handle pulled by hand, the kind of piece that ends up living on the table. Soft charcoal black outside and glossy inside, so it rinses clean. It pours water without a drip and holds an armful of wild flowers just as well.","materialNotes":["Wheel-thrown stoneware, hand-pulled handle","Matte charcoal glaze outside, clear gloss inside","Holds 1 litre","Food-safe","Hand-wash recommended"],"careNote":"Hand-wash to keep the matte surface soft. A drop of oil on a cloth brings back its depth.","batchSize":14,"stock":6,"releasedAt":"2026-08-29"},{"id":"2dd91cd5-9d71-43e1-a103-5e8c7d8eda2a","slug":"lull-plate","number":5,"name":"Lull Plate","category":"plates","glazeName":"Terracotta","glazeColor":"#A8553A","rimColor":null,"form":"plate","finish":"satin","speckled":false,"price":48,"dimensions":"Ø 260 × 25 mm","weight":"0.8 kg","description":"A flat dinner plate with a gently raised rim that keeps sauces where they belong. The terracotta glaze is fired to a soft satin, warm under candlelight and quiet on a white tablecloth. Made for slow dinners that run late.","materialNotes":["Wheel-thrown and trimmed stoneware","Terracotta satin glaze","Food-safe","Dishwasher-safe"],"careNote":"Dishwasher-safe. If you stack them for years, a napkin between plates keeps the glaze unmarked.","batchSize":14,"stock":6,"releasedAt":"2026-09-19"},{"id":"6ef44889-71cc-407c-b67c-dc81ceb57524","slug":"stem-bottle","number":6,"name":"Stem Bottle","category":"vases","glazeName":"Speckled cream","glazeColor":"#E6DCC4","rimColor":null,"form":"bottle","finish":"satin","speckled":true,"price":64,"dimensions":"Ø 70 × 230 mm","weight":"0.6 kg","description":"A slim bottle for a single stem, thrown in two parts and joined at the shoulder. The speckles are iron in the clay rising through the cream glaze in the kiln, so no two bottles carry the same pattern. It looks finished even when it stands empty.","materialNotes":["Speckled stoneware, thrown in two parts","Cream satin glaze","Watertight","Hand-wash only"],"careNote":"Rinse with a bottle brush and dry upside down. Fresh water every two days keeps a stem longer.","batchSize":14,"stock":6,"releasedAt":"2026-10-01"}],"workshops":[{"id":"9653321c-34bf-4ef6-ae77-65bb0828b1df","slug":"intro-to-the-wheel","name":"Intro to the Wheel","duration":"2 hours","price":55,"priceNote":"per person","description":"Two hours on a wheel of your own. We centre, open and pull together until something stands up by itself, then trim, glaze and fire your favourite piece for you.","capacity":8,"spotsLeft":3,"spotLabel":"places","nextSession":"2026-10-17T08:00:00.0